  // Master of Pendulum Structure Deck (TCG prefix SDMP), the TCG equivalent of
  // OCG "Structure Deck: Master of Pendulum" (SD29). 43 cards: 40 Main + 3 Extra.
  // NA release December 4, 2015 (EU December 3, 2015). Cover cards: Odd-Eyes
  // Absolute Dragon + Odd-Eyes Meteorburst Dragon. All names verified exactly
  // against cards.cdb via `node bin/ygo.js card`.
  "name": "Master of Pendulum (SDMP)",
  "category": "structure",
  "format": "classic",
  "manual": "PENDULUM MECHANICS (this is the library's only Pendulum deck). Pendulum Monsters double as Spells: place one in your left Pendulum Zone and one in your right, each showing a blue Pendulum Scale number. With a low scale L on one side and a high scale R on the other, ONCE per turn you Pendulum Summon any number of monsters at once whose Levels are strictly between L and R — from your hand, AND any face-up Pendulum Monsters sitting in your Extra Deck. The payoff loop: a Pendulum Monster that would go to the GY from the field instead lands FACE-UP in your Extra Deck, so you re-summon the same board again next turn. This deck runs two 1<->8 scale pairs — Stargazer Magician (scale 1) + Timegazer Magician (scale 8), and Dragonpulse Magician (1) + Dragonpit Magician (8) — both of which open the full Level 2-7 range, enough for the entire lineup including Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon (Lv7).\n\nCORE COMBO — set a scale, then swarm.\n1) OPEN with Performapal Skullcrobat Joker: Normal Summon it to search ANY Performapal, Magician Pendulum, or Odd-Eyes monster from Deck — your best turn-1 card, it digs to whatever scale piece you're missing.\n2) COMPLETE THE SCALE fast: Wisdom-Eye Magician's Pendulum Effect destroys itself (needs a Magician/Performapal in the other zone) to place any Magician Pendulum Monster from Deck straight into a Pendulum Zone. Pendulum Call discards 1 card to add TWO different-named Magician Pendulums from Deck to hand, and locks your Magician scales against card-effect destruction. Sky Iris (Field) searches an Odd-Eyes by destroying one of your own cards (blow up a spent scale you already used this turn) and stops the opponent targeting your Pendulum-Zone cards.\n3) PENDULUM SUMMON the board: with a 1/8 scale up, drop Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon plus beaters (Chaos Hunter, Fusilier Dragon, the Level-4 Performapals) from hand in one shot, reclaiming any Pendulum Monsters already face-up in your Extra Deck.\n\nREMOVAL ENGINE (the Dragon-Magician scale is also disruption): while a Magician sits in your OTHER zone, Dragonpulse Magician's Pendulum Effect discards a Pendulum Monster to destroy a face-up monster, and Dragonpit Magician's discards to destroy a Spell/Trap. So a Dragonpulse(1)/Dragonpit(8) scale is simultaneously your scale AND two shots of removal each turn (fuel the discards with dead Pendulums — you get them back from the Extra Deck).\n\nEXTRA DECK PAYOFFS — one of each Summon type:\n- XYZ: overlay two Level-7s (Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon + a second Lv7 you Pendulum Summoned, e.g. Dragonpit) into Odd-Eyes Absolute Dragon.\n- SYNCHRO: a Tuner (Nobledragon Magician, Magna Drago, or X-Saber Airbellum / Re-Cover) + non-Tuners into Odd-Eyes Meteorburst Dragon.\n- FUSION: Polymerization fuses Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon + any Spellcaster into Rune-Eyes Pendulum Dragon (Lv8, 3000 ATK) for multi-attacks. Oafdragon Magician recycles a Magician/Odd-Eyes Pendulum from GY or Extra Deck to grind the loop.\n\nWEAKNESSES (short): you brick if you draw only high scales or only low scales — you need one of each to Summon. Floodgates and heavy backrow that stop Special Summons shut the engine off, and there are no hand traps to fight back. Targeted destruction of an uncovered scale stalls you a turn (Timegazer protects one Pendulum-Zone card from effect destruction, Pendulum Call and Sky Iris cover the rest).",
  "sources": [
